---
title: "parse_and_verify_accumulator_updates (Pyth Sui Contracts)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_init: update_size = deserialize_u8(cursor), price_info_updates = []
    q_init --> q_loop: update_size > 0
    q_loop --> q_deser_msg: true
    q_loop --> [*]: false, return price_info_updates
    q_deser_msg --> q_parse: message_size = deserialize_u16, message = deserialize_vector
    q_parse --> q_price: message_cur = cursor::new(message)
    q_price --> q_push: price_info = parse_price_feed_message(message_cur, clock)
    q_push --> q_verify: push_back(price_info_updates, price_info)
    q_verify --> q_check_proof: merkle_tree::is_proof_valid(cursor, merkle_root, message)
    q_check_proof --> q_abort: false, abort E_INVALID_PROOF
    q_check_proof --> q_dec: true
    q_dec --> q_loop: update_size = update_size - 1

    note right of q_check_proof
        INV-001: every price update must have a valid Merkle proof against the root
        INV-002: message is parsed BEFORE proof verification (parse then verify)
        INV-003: proof is consumed from the same cursor as the updates
    end note
